WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.830
PROFESSOR 1: When you hear
the word quality, what are

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.680
some specific things that come to mind?

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:13.180
And whether that could be a
particular patient experience

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:19.870
or a hospital experience that you were
at that helped you have a better--

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.620
better articulate your own
thoughts on what quality is.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.540
PROFESSOR 2: Quality
is behind everything.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:31.120
If we take now health
infrastructure, I have

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.370
that experience of contracting
people to build a hospital.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.440
And they build it in the wrong way.

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:46.910
And imagine that it delayed the work
of health professional for six months.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.400
We delay six months.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:53.080
How many death are we going to have
because health professionals were

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.560
there and were not able to give care?

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.600
That's one.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:01.550
Now, the money we lose because
we have to destroy and rebuild,

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.840
and the time we lose,
it's behind everything.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.700
All the chain of service
and all the tools

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:16.700
we need to have to give the
proper service, behind all this,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:24.950
starting with education, continue with
the quality, the behavior you have.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:28.880
This is also something
that is very important.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.150
All along that chain,
from infrastructure,

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:36.470
from the type of staff you have,
from the type of medicine you use,

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.560
for the equipment you use
to give that medicine,

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:43.040
from the way you talk to
the patient and you explain

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.230
and dialogue with the patient, from the
way you make the patient participate

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:53.060
in whole health, and from the way
you plan with the patient the way

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.580
it's going to--

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:59.250
the thing is going to pass through
to recover, or at which extent

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:04.850
he will recover, to make him participate
in the future handicap management

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:05.780
he will have.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.759
All this need quality.

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:13.130
And if you miss one
point, either you will

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:16.810
see the patient will not contribute
to his part for his own health,

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:23.360
will not own his own health, or will
be harmed by what you are doing,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.370
or by what others are doing.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:31.140
So that means, at all
stage, you need people

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:40.490
to enter in the job to do the job,
to conclude the job with quality.

